course: dictionary
lesson: 7033
title: One word, three meanings: particular
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. «Particular» is one of them. Ask yourself: is it talking about one certain thing, something special, or a fussy person?
explain: In «on that particular day», particular means one certain day, not any other day. In «of particular importance», it means special, more than usual. Read the words around it and the meaning will often click.
explain: «He's very particular about his food» means he is fussy and cares a lot about details. The word «about» after particular is a strong clue. Swap in your meaning to check: does it still make sense?
explain: Particulars, with an s, is a formal word for the details or facts about something. You may see it in a form or a report.
fact: Particular means one certain thing, not any other: «on that particular day».
fact: Particular can mean special or more than usual: «of particular importance».
fact: «In particular» means especially, as in «elephants fear mice in particular».
fact: «Particular about» something means fussy, as in «don't be particular», which means don't be fussy.
fact: «Nothing in particular» means nothing special.
exercise: «We are meeting on that particular day, the one in the diary.» What does particular mean here? | Very happy | Fussy about days | Long and tiring | *One certain day, not any other
exercise: «Ella is very particular about her food.» What does particular mean? | Special and important | One certain food | Quiet and shy | *Fussy, and careful about details
exercise: «The shop has nothing in particular on sale today.» What does nothing in particular mean? | Something very special | A particular case in maths | Lots of different things | *Nothing special
test: «There is no good evidence that elephants fear mice in particular.» What does in particular mean here? | Only at night | *Especially | Quietly | Once
test: The form asks for the particulars of the car. What are the particulars? | A loud noise from the engine | *The details or facts about it | The price, and nothing else | The paint colour only
exam: Which meaning of particular fits «of particular importance»? | Fussy | Quiet | *Special, more than usual | One certain thing, not any other
